  abstract = "Most members of the Pseudoalteromonas genus have been isolated
              from living surfaces as members of epiphytic and epizooic
              microbiomes on marine macroorganisms. Commonly Pseudoalteromonas
              isolates are reported as a source of bioactive exoproducts, i.e.,
              secondary metabolites, such as exopolymeric substances and
              extracellular enzymes. The experimental conditions for the
              production of these agents are commonly associated with sessile
