              utilizes epithelial-derived nitrate, whereas nitrate in the niche
              occupied by S. Typhimurium is derived from phagocytic infiltrates.
              Surprisingly, avirulent S. Typhimurium was shown to be unable to
              utilize epithelial-derived nitrate because its chemotaxis
              receptors McpB and McpC exclude the pathogen from the niche
              occupied by E. coli. In contrast, E. coli invades the niche
