  number   =  18,
  pages    = "7745--7766",
  abstract = "Pseudomonas putida is a Gram-negative, rod-shaped bacterium that
              can be encountered in diverse ecological habitats. This ubiquity
              is traced to its remarkably versatile metabolism, adapted to
