              nucleotide variants in genomes of several organisms. In the
              present study, we have investigated single nucleotide polymorphism
              (SNP) in ten multi-antibiotic resistant Pseudomonas aeruginosa
              clinical isolates. All the draft genomes were submitted to Rapid
              Annotations using Subsystems Technology (RAST) web server and the
              predicted protein sequences were used for comparison.
              Non-synonymous single nucleotide polymorphism (nsSNP) found in the
              clinical isolates compared to the reference genome (PAO1), and the
