  journal  = "MBio",
  pages    = "e0041722",
  abstract = "Pseudomonas aeruginosa is an opportunistic bacterial pathogen that
              exhibits pathogenicity in an unusually broad range of plants and
              animals, and it is of interest to study the roles of particular
              virulence-related factors in diverse hosts. The production of many
              P. aeruginosa virulence factors is under the control of a quorum
