  volume   =  22,
  number   =  23,
  abstract = "σ54 factor (RpoN), a type of transcriptional regulatory factor, is
              widely found in pathogenic bacteria. It binds to core RNA
              polymerase (RNAP) and regulates the transcription of many
              functional genes in an enhancer-binding protein (EBP)-dependent
              manner. σ54 has two conserved functional domains: the
              activator-interacting domain located at the N-terminal and the
