              Braubach, Peter and Jonigk, Danny and Haverich, Axel and Warnecke,
              Gregor and Häussler, Susanne",
  journal  = "Nat. Commun.",
  volume   =  10,
  number   =  1,
  pages    =  3397,
  abstract = "Previous studies have demonstrated substantial genetic
              diversification of Pseudomonas aeruginosa across sub-compartments
              in cystic fibrosis (CF) lungs. Here, we isolate P. aeruginosa from
              five different sampling areas in the upper and lower airways of an
              explanted CF lung, analyze ex vivo transcriptional profiles by
              RNA-seq, and use colony re-sequencing and deep population
              sequencing to determine the genetic diversity within and across
              the various sub-compartments. We find that, despite genetic
              variation, the ex vivo transcriptional profiles of P. aeruginosa
              populations inhabiting different regions of the CF lung are
              similar. Although we cannot estimate the extent to which the
              transcriptional response recorded here actually reflects the in
              vivo transcriptomes, our results indicate that there may be a
              common in vivo transcriptional profile in the CF lung environment.",
  month    =  jul,
  year     =  2019,
  language = "en"
}

@ARTICLE{Trouillon2022-ug,
