               10 years) field- and lab-based monitoring data collected at
               high-temporal (every hour) and spatial (up to 6 depths)
               resolution. In addition, we set up a redox experiment where we
               manipulated the soil temperature (ST) by diel temperature cycles
               to assess the EH response. Diel fluctuations were absent for
               laboratory experiments with ΔEH of a few mV (daily EH-max – daily
               EH-min), but we found pronounced fluctuations up to ∼100 mV for
               field investigations. The spatiotemporal pattern in EH
               fluctuations was amplified in the topsoil during the summer
               months concomitant with ST. We showed for the first time that
