              most of the O2 that diffused into the mat was used to oxidize
              sulfide, with O2 respiration of minor importance. During the day,
              the internal mat processes of sulfate reduction and O2 respiration
              generated as much or more inorganic carbon (DIC) for primary
              production as diffusion into the mat. Also, oxygenic
              photosynthesis was the most important process of carbon fixation,
              although anoxygenic photosynthesis may have been important at low
              light levels during some times of the year. At night, the DIC lost
