              across the mat/brine interface indicated that carbon with an
              oxidation state of greater than zero was taken up by the mat
              during the day and liberated from the mat at night. Overall,
              carbon with an average oxidation state of near zero accumulated in
              the mat. Both carbon fixation and carbon oxidation rates varied
