  volume   =  4,
  number   =  1,
  pages    =  1,
  abstract = "Pure, soluble and functional proteins are of high demand in modern
              biotechnology. Natural protein sources rarely meet the
              requirements for quantity, ease of isolation or price and hence
              recombinant technology is often the method of choice. Recombinant
              cell factories are constantly employed for the production of
              protein preparations bound for downstream purification and
              processing. Eschericia coli is a frequently used host, since it
