              genetic analysis, to identify new gene products involved in
              intracellular killing. A random genetic screen led us to identify
              the role of Vps13F in intracellular killing of Klebsiella
              pneumoniae. Vps13F knock-out (KO) cells exhibited a delayed
              intracellular killing of K. pneumoniae, although the general
              organization of the phagocytic and endocytic pathway appeared
