  journal  = "J. Bacteriol.",
  pages    = "JB0042221",
  abstract = "Staphylococcus aureus is a versatile opportunistic pathogen whose
              success is driven by its ability to adapt to diverse environments
              and host-imposed stresses. Two-component signal transduction
              systems, such as ArlRS, often mediate these adaptations. Loss of
              ArlRS or the response regulator ArlR alone impairs the ability of
