  journal  = "ISME J.",
  abstract = "Trophic interactions play a central role in driving microbial
              community assembly and function. In gut or soil ecosystems,
              successful inoculants are always facilitated by efficient
              colonization; however, the metabolite exchanges between inoculants
              and resident bacteria are rarely studied, particularly in the
