  volume   =  6,
  number   =  1,
  pages    = "28--34",
  abstract = "Pseudomonas aeruginosa produces the toxic secondary metabolite
              hydrogen cyanide (HCN) at high cell population densities and low
              aeration. Here, we investigated the impact of HCN as a signal in
              cell-cell communication by comparing the transcriptome of the
              wild-type strain PAO1 to that of an HCN-negative mutant under
