  journal  = "J. Bacteriol.",
  volume   =  201,
  number   =  12,
  abstract = "Pseudomonas aeruginosa frequently resides among ethanol-producing
              microbes, making its response to the microbially produced
              concentrations of ethanol relevant to understanding its biology.
              Our transcriptome analysis found that genes involved in trehalose
              metabolism were induced by low concentrations of ethanol, and
