               unique ability to grow in the presence or in the absence of
               oxygen. and are thus well-adapted to these changing conditions
               which may constitute an underestimated selective advantage for
               infection. In the WHO antibiotic-resistant ``priority pathogens''
               list, facultative anaerobes are overrepresented (8 among 12
               listed pathogens), consistent with clinical studies performed in
               populations particularly susceptible to infectious diseases.
               Bacteria aerobic respiratory chain plays a central role in oxygen
               consumption, leading to the formation of hypoxic infectious sites
