  number    =  2,
  abstract  = "ABSTRACT Pseudomonas aeruginosa and Staphylococcus aureus are two
               of the most common coinfecting bacteria in human infections,
               including the cystic fibrosis (CF) lung. There is emerging
               evidence that coinfection with these microbes enhances disease
               severity and antimicrobial tolerance through direct interactions.
