               model based on an in vitro medium that mimics human CF lung
               secretions (synthetic CF sputum medium [SCFM2]) and allows
               time-resolved assessment of fitness and community spatial
               structure at the micrometer scale. Our results reveal that P.
               aeruginosa and S. aureus coexist as spatially structured
               communities in SCFM2 under static growth conditions, with S.
               aureus enriched at a distance of 3.5 μm from P. aeruginosa.
