               cross-talking, in multispecies biofilm, to signify the importance
               of such interactions on the initial formation and subsequent
               growth of these biofilms. Multispecies biofilms with their
               species heterogeneity are more resilient to antimicrobial agents
               than their single species biofilm counterparts and this
               characteristic is of particular interest when dealing with
