               falling off in sexual reactivity as temperature increases above
               the optimum, while variety 1 shows a sudden cessation of sexual
               reactivity at a temperature only 2° above the optimum.It is thus
               possible to distinguish these four varieties of P. aurelia not
               only by their mating types, but also by the sexual responses to
