              begins with a number of changes in the ligand-binding cavity upon
              cAMP binding. These subtle structural changes and numerous
              non-bonding interactions between cAMP, the N-domain residues, and
              the C-domain helices demonstrate that the N-domain hairpin loop
              acts as a structural mediator of the allosteric switch. Based on
              the CRP.N(6)-cAMP crystal structure, binding of N(6)-cAMP with a
              bulkier methylphenylethyl extension from the N6 atom stabilizes
              the cAMP-binding domain, N-domain hairpin, and C-terminal domain
