              susceptibility profiles. Here, we observe that exposure to P.
              aeruginosa exoproducts leads to an increase in intracellular
              norfloxacin accumulation by S. aureus We previously showed that P.
              aeruginosa supernatant dissipates the S. aureus membrane
              potential, and furthermore, depletion of the S. aureus proton
              motive force recapitulates the effect of the P. aeruginosa PA14
              supernatant on shifting norfloxacin sensitivity profiles of
