              controls in B. dolosa strain AU0158. Using a fixK-lacZ reporter we
              found that FixLJ was activated in low oxygen in multiple BCC
              species. In a murine pneumonia model, the B. dolosa fixLJ deletion
              mutant was cleared faster from the lungs and spleen than wild-type
              B. dolosa strain AU0158 at 7 days post infection. Interestingly,
              the fixLJ deletion mutant made more biofilm, albeit with altered
              structure, but was less motile than strain AU0158. Using RNA-seq
              with in vitro grown bacteria, we found ~11\% of the genome was
              differentially expressed in the fixLJ deletion mutant relative to
              strain AU0158. Multiple flagella-associated genes were
