              factors other than flagella caused the phenotype of decreased
              persistence. We found the fixLJ deletion mutant to be less
              invasive in human lung epithelial and macrophage-like cells. In
              conclusion, B. dolosa fixLJ is a global regulator that controls
              biofilm formation, motility, intracellular invasion/persistence,
