  volume   =  2,
  pages    =  100015,
  abstract = "Biofilms are the primary cause of clinical bacterial infections
              and are impervious to typical amounts of antibiotics,
              necessitating very high doses for elimination. Therefore, it is
              imperative to have suitable methods for characterization to
              develop novel methods of treatment that can complement or replace
              existing approaches using significantly lower doses of
