              proline, which is adjacent to the phosphoryl acceptor histidine,
              contributes to helical bending, which is essential for the
              autokinase and phosphatase activities. Together, the elegant
              architecture of VicK with a signal transducer and sensor domain
              suggests a model where DHp helical bending and a CA swing movement
              are likely coordinated for autokinase activation.",
  month    =  feb,
  year     =  2013,
  language = "en"
}

@ARTICLE{Bhate2015-rq,
  title    = "Signal transduction in histidine kinases: insights from new
              structures",
  author   = "Bhate, Manasi P and Molnar, Kathleen S and Goulian, Mark and
              DeGrado, William F",
  journal  = "Structure",
  volume   =  23,
  number   =  6,
  pages    = "981--994",
  abstract = "Histidine kinases (HKs) are major players in bacterial signaling.
