              immunohistology (IH), respectively. The results were additionally
              compared with those obtained by polymerase chain reaction (PCR)
              for EBV-DNA detection. EBV was detected by EBER-ISH in 67\% of the
              HD cases and in 25\% of the control group cases consisting of
              normal lymph nodes. The results of PCR performed on cases with
              amplifiable DNA were overall congruent with those obtained by
              EBER-ISH. With respect to the cellular localization of EBV, four
              categories of HD could be established: (a) cases with EBV-infected
