              communities. Within these communities metabolic activities are
              integrated, and developmental sequences, not unlike those of
              multicellular organisms, can be detected. These structural
              adaptations and interrelationships are made possible by the
              expression of sets of genes that result in phenotypes that differ
              profoundly from those of planktonically grown cells of the same
              species. Molecular and microscopic evidence suggest the existence
