              detection of sharp gradients of pH within microbial biofilms.",
  month    =  aug,
  year     =  1999,
  language = "en"
}

@ARTICLE{Battin2001-fm,
  title    = "Phylogenetic and functional heterogeneity of sediment biofilms
              along environmental gradients in a glacial stream",
  author   = "Battin, T J and Wille, A and Sattler, B and Psenner, R",
  journal  = "Appl. Environ. Microbiol.",
  volume   =  67,
  number   =  2,
  pages    = "799--807",
  abstract = "We used in situ hybridization with fluorescently labeled
              rRNA-targeted oligonucleotide probes concurrently with
              measurements of bacterial carbon production, biomass, and
              extracellular polymeric substances (EPS) to describe the bacterial
              community in sediments along a glacial stream. The abundance of
