              Actinobacteria, Cyanobacteria) are present in these habitats along
              with eukaryotes such as microscopic green algae and ascomycetous
              fungi. The subaerial biofilm inhabitants have adapted to
              desiccation, solar radiation, and other environmental challenges
              by developing protective, melanized cell walls, assuming
