  volume   =  8,
  number   =  5,
  pages    = "953--962",
  abstract = "Cross-feeding interactions, in which bacterial cells exchange
              costly metabolites to the benefit of both interacting partners,
              are very common in the microbial world. However, it generally
              remains unclear what maintains this type of interaction in the
              presence of non-cooperating types. We investigate this problem
