              genetic strategies for a division of labor can promote collective
              biofilm formation in the soil bacterium Bacillus subtilis. In this
              species, biofilm matrix consists of two major components,
              exopolysaccharides (EPSs) and TasA. We observed that clonal groups
              of B. subtilis phenotypically segregate into three subpopulations
