  abstract = "Microbes live in ever-changing environments where they need to
              adapt their metabolism to different nutrient conditions. Many
              studies have characterized the response of genetically identical
              cells to nutrient switches in homogeneous cultures; however, in
              nature, microbes often live in spatially structured groups such as
              biofilms where cells can create metabolic gradients by consuming
