              populations of Escherichia coli in microfluidic chambers and
              studying a switch from glucose to acetate at the single-cell
              level. Before the switch, cells vary in their metabolic activity:
              some grow on glucose, while others cross-feed on acetate. After
              the switch, only few cells can resume growth after a period of
              lag. The probability to resume growth depends on a cells'
              phenotype prior to the switch: it is highest for cells
              cross-feeding on acetate, while it depends in a non-monotonic way
