              co-incubation with energy metabolism inhibitors. Although
              oxidative phosphorylation is a promising target space for drug
              development, a better understanding of the link between energy
              metabolism and antibiotic-induced mycobacterial death is essential
              to develop potent drug combinations for the treatment of
              tuberculosis.",
  month    =  feb,
  year     =  2019,
  keywords = "ATP; Bedaquiline; Mycobacterium tuberculosis; Q203; Telacebec;
              antagonism; antibiotics; cell death; oxidative phosphorylation;
