  author   = "Nadell, Carey D and Ricaurte, Deirdre and Yan, Jing and Drescher,
              Knut and Bassler, Bonnie L",
  journal  = "Elife",
  volume   =  6,
  abstract = "Bacteria often live in biofilms, which are microbial communities
              surrounded by a secreted extracellular matrix. Here, we
              demonstrate that hydrodynamic flow and matrix organization
              interact to shape competitive dynamics in Pseudomonas aeruginosa
              biofilms. Irrespective of initial frequency, in competition with
