              and is influenced by the metabolic phenotypes of the infecting
              pathogens. Ultra performance liquid chromatography with mass
              spectrometry detection was used to measure agmatine in human
              sputum samples from patients with cystic fibrosis, spent
              supernatant from clinical sputum isolates, and from
              bronchoalvelolar lavage fluid from mice infected with P.
