              Pseudomonas aeruginosa biofilms were grown in drip flow reactors
              on a medium composed to mimic the exudate from a chronic wound.
              After 4 days, the biofilm was 114 μm thick with 9.45 log10 CFU
              cm-2 These biofilms exhibited tolerance, relative to
              exponential-phase planktonic cells, to subsequent treatment with
