  volume   =  1798,
  number   =  6,
  pages    = "1281--1284",
  abstract = "During respiration, it is accepted that oxygen diffuses passively
              from the lung alveolar spaces through the respiratory epithelium
              until reaching the pulmonary capillaries, where blood is
              oxygenated. It is also widely assumed that pulmonary surfactant, a
              lipid–protein complex secreted into alveolar spaces, has a main
