              high-throughput sequencing. Changes in frequency of Tn inserts
              into the P. aeruginosa genome were used to quantify in vivo
              fitness resulting from loss of a gene. 636 genes had <10
              sequencing reads in LB, thus defined as unable to grow in this
              medium. During in vivo infection there were major losses of
