  journal  = "Nat. Commun.",
  volume   =  10,
  number   =  1,
  pages    =  1697,
  abstract = "Cell-free transcription-translation systems have great potential
              for biosensing, yet the range of detectable chemicals is limited.
              Here we provide a workflow to expand the range of molecules
              detectable by cell-free biosensors through combining synthetic
              metabolic cascades with transcription factor-based networks. These
              hybrid cell-free biosensors have a fast response time, strong
              signal response, and a high dynamic range. In addition, they are
              capable of functioning in a variety of complex media, including
