  journal  = "Nat. Commun.",
  volume   =  12,
  number   =  1,
  pages    =  1986,
  abstract = "Many bacteria use the second messenger cyclic diguanylate
              (c-di-GMP) to control motility, biofilm production and virulence.
              Here, we identify a thermosensory diguanylate cyclase (TdcA) that
              modulates temperature-dependent motility, biofilm development and
