  volume   =  481,
  number   =  7379,
  pages    = "76--80",
  abstract = "Discriminating among sensory stimuli is critical for animal
              survival. This discrimination is particularly essential when
              evaluating whether a stimulus is noxious or innocuous. From
              insects to humans, transient receptor potential (TRP) channels are
              key transducers of thermal, chemical and other sensory cues. Many
