              nm instead of the typical 408 nm and a steep hydroxymet transition
              at pH > or = 9.3; these properties indicate a pentacoordinated
              high-spin ferric heme and suggest a sterically hindered
              hydrophobic heme pocket lacking a distal (E7) histidine. FixL is
              the first member of a new class of heme proteins, the heme-based
              sensors, distinct from the oxygen carriers and electron
              transporters. We expect that some of the novel properties of FixL
