              changes within the homotypic dimer of the input domain (PAS, GAF,
              HAMP, etc.), which are structurally coupled with the arrangement
              of the GGDEF domains via a rigid coiled-coil linker.
              Alternatively, phosphorylation of a Rec input domain can drive
              GGDEF dimerization. Both mechanisms allow modular combination of
              input and output function that appears advantageous for evolution
