  number   =  4,
  pages    = "688--702",
  abstract = "Cellulose, whose production is controlled by c-di-GMP, is a
              commonly found exopolysaccharide in bacterial biofilms.
              Pseudomonas syringae pv. tomato (Pto) DC3000, a model organism for
              molecular studies of plant-pathogen interactions, carries the
