  pages     =  1203,
  abstract  = "Pseudomonas chlororaphis PA23 was isolated from the rhizosphere
               of soybeans and identified as a biocontrol bacterium against
               Sclerotinia sclerotiorum, a fungal plant pathogen. This bacterium
               produces a number of secondary metabolites, including
               phenazine-1-carboxylic acid, 2-hydroxyphenazine, pyrrolnitrin
