               polymers as carbon and energy storage compounds under
               nutrient-limited conditions. Pseudomonads like P. chlororaphis
               metabolize glucose via the Entner-Doudoroff and Pentose Phosphate
               pathways, which provide precursors for phenazine production.
               Mutants defective in phenazine (PHZ; PA23-63), PRN (PA23-8), or
               both (PA23-63-1) accumulated higher concentrations of PHAs than
               the wild-type strain (PA23) when cultured in Ramsay's Minimal
               Medium with glucose or octanoic acid as the carbon source.
               Expression levels of six pha genes, phaC1, phaZ, phaC2, phaD,
               phaF, and phaI, were compared with wild type PA23 by quantitative
               real time polymerase chain reaction (qPCR). The qPCR studies
