  journal  = "MBio",
  volume   =  10,
  number   =  1,
  abstract = "Pseudomonas aeruginosa is an opportunistic pathogen and the
              leading cause of morbidity and mortality in cystic fibrosis (CF)
              patients. P. aeruginosa infections are difficult to treat due to a
              number of antibiotic resistance mechanisms and the organism's
              propensity to form multicellular biofilms. Epidemic strains of P.
