              strains isolated from different CF patients. In addition, we found
              that these phage-like pyocins are inhibitory against mature
              biofilms of susceptible strains. This highlights the potential of
              R-pyocins as antimicrobial and antibiofilm agents at a time when
              new antimicrobial therapies are desperately needed.",
  month    =  jan,
  year     =  2019,
  keywords = "Pseudomonas aeruginosa ; bacteriocins; biofilms; cystic fibrosis;
              pyocins",
  language = "en"
}

