  publisher = "Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH \& Co. KGaA",
  address   = "Weinheim, Germany",
  volume    =  238,
  pages     = "277--291",
  abstract  = "Summary Overview The biofilm mode of life is common to almost all
               microorganisms on Earth, be it continuously or as part of their
               life cycle. Biofilm phenomena are very diverse. They range from
               films on solid surfaces, aggregates at the water-atmosphere
               interface to flocs as ?floating biofilms,? microbial mats, and
