              Seung",
  journal  = "Chem. Soc. Rev.",
  volume   =  48,
  number   =  3,
  pages    = "771--813",
  abstract = "Hypoxia is a state of low oxygen tension found in numerous solid
              tumours. It is typically associated with abnormal vasculature,
              which results in a reduced supply of oxygen and nutrients, as well
              as impaired delivery of drugs. The hypoxic nature of tumours often
              leads to the development of localized heterogeneous environments
              characterized by variable oxygen concentrations, relatively low
              pH, and increased levels of reactive oxygen species (ROS). The
              hypoxic heterogeneity promotes tumour invasiveness, metastasis,
