              reaction stoichiometry and pH. With Fe(0), strain 4t3-1-2LB
              completely reduced fumarate to succinate and increased the Fe(0)
              corrosion rate (7.0 ± 0.6)-fold in comparison to that of abiotic
              controls (based on the succinate-versus-abiotic hydrogen formation
              rate). Fumarate reduction by strain 4t3-1-2LB was, at least in
              part, supported by chemical hydrogen formation on Fe(0).
              Filter-sterilized spent medium increased the hydrogen generation
              rate only 1.5-fold, and thus extracellular hydrogenase enzymes
              appear to be insufficient to explain the enhanced corrosion rate.
              Electrochemical measurements suggested that strain 4t3-1-2LB did
