              the absence of phosphofructokinase activity, a cyclic flux from
              the ED pathway to the upper Embden-Meyerhof-Parnas (EMP) pathway
              was responsible for routing glucose-derived carbons to the
              non-oxidative pentose phosphate (PP) pathway. Consistent with the
              lack of annotated genes in P. protegens Pf-5 for the transport or
