  volume   =  30,
  number   =  13,
  pages    = "1651--1696",
  abstract = "SIGNIFICANCE: The successful adaptation of microorganisms to
              ever-changing environments depends, to a great extent, on their
              ability to maintain redox homeostasis. To effectively maintain the
              redox balance, cells have developed a variety of strategies mainly
              coordinated by a battery of transcriptional regulators through
              diverse mechanisms. Recent Advances: This comprehensive review
