  journal  = "Elife",
  volume   =  7,
  abstract = "Nitric oxide (NO) is released into the air by NO-producing
              organisms; however, it is unclear if animals utilize NO as a
              sensory cue. We show that C. elegans avoids Pseudomonas aeruginosa
              (PA14) in part by detecting PA14-produced NO. PA14 mutants
