  volume   =  14,
  number   =  1,
  pages    = "e1006804",
  abstract = "Resistance-nodulation-division (RND) efflux systems are ubiquitous
              transporters in Gram-negative bacteria that are essential for
              antibiotic resistance. The RND efflux systems also contribute to
              diverse phenotypes independent of antimicrobial resistance, but
              the mechanism by which they affect most of these phenotypes is
