              and V. cholerae virulence. RNA sequencing revealed that the loss
              of RND efflux affected the activation state of periplasmic sensing
              systems including the virulence regulator ToxR. Activation of ToxR
              in an RND null mutant resulted in ToxR-dependent transcription of
              the LysR-family regulator leuO. Increased leuO transcription
              resulted in the repression of the ToxR virulence regulon and
