              deletion restored virulence factor production in an RND-null
              mutant, but not its ability to colonize infant mice; suggesting
              that RND efflux was epistatic to virulence factor production for
              colonization. The periplasmic sensing domain of ToxR was required
              for the induction of leuO transcription in the RND null mutant,
              suggesting that ToxR responded to metabolites that accumulated in
              the periplasm. Our results suggest that ToxR represses virulence
              factor production in response to metabolites that are normally
              effluxed from the cell by the RND transporters. We propose that
              impaired RND efflux results in periplasmic metabolite
              accumulation, which then activates periplasmic sensors including
