              effector/target systems.IMPORTANCE c-di-GMP signaling in bacteria
              is believed to occur via changes in cellular c-di-GMP levels
              controlled by antagonistic and potentially interacting pairs of
              diguanylate cyclases (DGCs) and c-di-GMP phosphodiesterases
              (PDEs). Our systematic analysis of protein-protein interaction
