              determined using nuclear magnetic resonance spectroscopy. We
              conducted whole genome sequencing for the identification of the
              gene cluster(s) believed to be responsible for phenazine
              biosynthesis in order to map its corresponding pathway, in
              addition to bioinformatics analysis to assess the potential of S.
