              µM). In contrast, >50\% of P. aeruginosa isolates from chronic CF
              pulmonary infections expressed increased levels of alginate and
              mucoidy both under iron-limiting and iron-replete conditions
              (i.e., iron-constitutive phenotype). No single iron regulatory
              factor (e.g., Fur, PvdS) was associated with this loss of
              iron-regulated alginate expression and mucoidy in these CF
              isolates. However, the loss of only pyoverdine production, or its
              uptake, abrogated the ability of P. aeruginosa to produce a robust
              biofilm that represents the Psl-type of biofilm. In contrast, we
