              elements of the biofilm matrix and are implied in surface adhesion
              and biofilm organization, but their contributions to the
              resistance properties of biofilms remain largely elusive. Using a
              combination of static and continuous-flow biofilm experiments we
              show that Psl, one major polysaccharide in the Pseudomonas
              aeruginosa biofilm matrix, provides a generic first line of
