  journal  = "Science",
  volume   =  357,
  number   =  6352,
  pages    = "713--717",
  abstract = "Contractile injection systems mediate bacterial cell-cell
              interactions by a bacteriophage tail-like structure. In contrast
              to extracellular systems, the type 6 secretion system (T6SS) is
              defined by intracellular localization and attachment to the
              cytoplasmic membrane. Here we used cryo-focused ion beam milling,
              electron cryotomography, and functional assays to study a T6SS in
              Amoebophilus asiaticus The in situ architecture revealed three
              modules, including a contractile sheath-tube, a baseplate, and an
