              factors, while affecting integrin binding and activation. In vitro
              and in vivo investigations point to redox reactions as targets for
              intervention in pulmonary fibrosis and related disorders, but
              studies in humans have been disappointing probably due to the
              narrow impact of the interventions tested, and our poor
