  abstract = "Bacteria possess molecular biosensors that enable responses to a
              variety of stressful conditions, including oxidative stress, toxic
              compounds, and interactions with other organisms, through
              elaborately coordinated regulation of gene expression. In
              Escherichia coli and related bacteria, the transcription factor
              SoxR functions as a sensor of oxidative stress and nitric oxide
              (NO). SoxR protein contains a [2Fe-2S] cluster essential for its
              transcription-enhancing activity, which is regulated by redox
              changes in the [2Fe-2S] cluster. We have explored the mechanistic
