              the interaction of E. coli and Pseudomonas aeruginosa SoxR with
              superoxide anion using a mutagenic approach. Despite the homology
              between E. coli SoxR and P. aeruginosa SoxR, the function of P.
              aeruginosa SoxR differs from that of E. coli. The substitution of
              E. coli SoxR lysine residues, located close to [2Fe-2S] clusters,
