              permeation through colony biofilms, indicated by a diffusion cell
              bioassay, demonstrated that there was no acceleration in bacterial
              killing once the antibiotics penetrated the biofilms. These
              results suggested that limited antibiotic diffusion is not the
              primary protective mechanism for these biofilms. Transmission
              electron microscopic observations of antibiotic-affected cells
              showed lysed, vacuolated, and elongated cells exclusively near the
