              spectinomycin, a bacteriostatic antibiotic, rescued the predation
              defect of the TA(-) mutant. In contrast, against Micrococcus
              luteus the TA(-) mutant exhibited no defect in ZOI or killing.
              Thus, TA plays a selective role on prey species. To extend these
              studies to other myxobacteria, the role of antibiotic
              corallopyronin production in predation was tested and also found
              to be required for Corallococcus coralloides killing on E. coli.
              Next, a role of TA production in myxobacterial fitness was
