              codons 3-5-fold, and this same effect was seen in other gene
              contexts. Therefore, IF3 is generally able to discriminate between
              efficient and inefficient codons in vivo, consistent with earlier
              in vitro observations. We discuss these observations as they
              relate to IF3 autoregulation and the mechanism of IF3 function.",
  month    =  jul,
  year     =  1996,
  language = "en"
}

