              band toward the oxic region typically return to the band within 16
              s following a U-shaped track. A detailed analysis of the tracks
              reveals that the cells must be able to sense the oxygen gradient
              perpendicular to their swimming direction. Thus, they can detect
              oxygen gradients along a distance of approximately 5 microm
              corresponding to the extension of their long axis. The observed
              behavior can be explained by the presence of two independent
