              all three components. The range of neurochemicals produced by
              probiotics includes neurochemicals for which receptor-based
              targets on immune and neuronal elements (intestinal and
              extra-intestinal) have been well characterized. Production of
              neurochemicals by probiotics therefore allows for their
              consideration as delivery vehicles for neuroactive compounds. This
              unifying microbial endocrinology-based hypothesis, which may
