  volume   =  79,
  number   =  23,
  pages    = "7142--7149",
  abstract = "Achromobacter xylosoxidans is an aerobic nonfermentative
              Gram-negative rod considered an important emerging pathogen among
              cystic fibrosis (CF) patients worldwide and among
              immunocompromised patients. This increased prevalence remains
              unexplained, and to date no environmental reservoir has been
