  pages    = "1661--1673",
  abstract = "Pyoverdines are siderophores produced by fluorescent Pseudomonads
              to acquire iron. At least 60 different pyoverdines produced by
              diverse strains have been chemically characterized. They all
              consist of a dihydroquinoline-type chromophore linked to a
              peptide. These peptides are of various lengths and the sequences
