              chronic P. aeruginosa CF lung infections. In the present study, we
              showed that it is possible to modulate the behavior of a highly
              adapted transmissible P. aeruginosa CF isolate at both the
              transcriptomic and phenotypic levels by introducing shear stress
              in a CF-like environment, driving it from a biofilm to a
              planktonic lifestyle. Consequently, the results obtained in this
