              of plant-pathogen interactions. In this review, we highlight the
              studies carried out so far on two model plant pathogens, namely
              Pseudomonas syringae and Hyaloperonospora arabidopsidis, and the
              involvement of the circadian clock in gating effector-triggered
              immunity and pathogen-associated molecular pattern-triggered
              immunity. We focus on how the circadian clock gates the expression
              of various stress-related transcripts in a prolific manner to
              enhance plant fitness. An understanding of this dynamic
              relationship between clock and stress will open up new avenues in
