              physiological evidence of the existence of a circadian pacemaker
              that controls the metabolism, photosynthesis, synchronized mass
              spawning, and calcification processes in symbiotic corals. In this
              review, we present current knowledge regarding the animal
              pacemaker and the symbiotic-algal pacemaker. We examine the
              evidence from behavioral, physiological, molecular, and
              evolutionary perspectives. We explain why symbiotic corals are an
