  volume   =  288,
  number   =  48,
  pages    = "34514--34528",
  abstract = "WhiB-like (Wbl) proteins are well known for their diverse roles in
              actinobacterial morphogenesis, cell division, virulence, primary
              and secondary metabolism, and intrinsic antibiotic resistance.
              Gene disruption experiments showed that three different
              Actinobacteria (Mycobacterium smegmatis, Streptomyces lividans,
