              amounts of blue pigment were produced by P. aeruginosa isolates
              when grown on nutrient agar media. Müller-Hinton agar was further
              used for growth, pigment production and sensitivity tests.
              P.aeruginosa isolates were grown in peptone water liquid medium by
              incubating at 37 0 C. for 24hrs. Then, culture tubes were shaken
              gently and centrifuged 10000rpm for 30 minutes to extract the
              supernatant. Using 5mL of the bacterial supernatant, 1mL of
              chloroform was added and shaken vigorously. The chloroform layer
              was removed (which should be on the bottom and turn blue to
