  booktitle = "Current Protocols in Microbiology",
  publisher = "John Wiley \& Sons, Inc.",
  abstract  = "Many bacteria can exist as surface-attached aggregations known as
               biofilms. Presented in this unit are several approaches for the
               study of these communities. The focus here is on static biofilm
               systems, which are particularly useful for examination of the
               early stages of biofilm formation, including initial adherence to
