              methyl group-containing substrates and some on acetate. The free
              energy change associated with methanogenesis from these compounds
              allows for the synthesis of 1 (acetate) to a maximum of only 2 mol
              of ATP under standard conditions while under environmental
              conditions less than one ATP can be synthesized. Therefore,
              methanogens live close to the thermodynamic limit. To cope with
