  volume   =  111,
  number   =  31,
  pages    = "11551--11556",
  abstract = "The phloem performs essential systemic functions in tracheophytes,
              yet little is known about its molecular genetic specification.
              Here we show that application of the peptide ligand
              CLAVATA3/embryo surrounding region 45 (CLE45) specifically
              inhibits specification of protophloem in Arabidopsis roots by
              locking the sieve element precursor cell in its preceding
              developmental state. CLE45 treatment, as well as viable transgenic
