              phase. Subcellular localization experiments indicated that Che
              proteins form signal transduction complexes at cell poles
              throughout growth. Cyan fluorescent protein (CFP)-tagged McpA, a
              stationary phase-expressed chemoreceptor, appeared and colocalized
              with yellow fluorescent protein (YFP)-tagged CheA when cells
              entered stationary phase. This indicates that P. aeruginosa
              chemotaxis protein complexes are subject to remoulding by
              chemoreceptor proteins that are expressed when cells stop growing.
              CheA-CFP and CheY2-YFP tagged proteins that were coexpressed in
