  abstract = "The high energetic requirements for nitrogen fixation and the
              extreme oxygen sensitivity of the nitrogenase enzyme impose
              physiological constraints on diazotrophy that necessitate
              stringent control of nitrogen fixation (nif) gene expression at
              the transcriptional level. In the gamma-subdivision of the
              Proteobacteria, this control is maintained by a regulatory complex
              comprising an enhancer-binding protein (NIFA), which activates
