  volume   =  45,
  pages    = "51--112",
  abstract = "In contrast to the bacterial assimilatory and membrane-associated,
              respiratory nitrate reductases that have been studied for many
              years, it is only recently that periplasmic nitrate reductases
              have attracted growing interest. Recent research has shown that
              these soluble proteins are widely distributed, but vary greatly
              between species. All of those so far studied include four
              essential components: the periplasmic molybdoprotein, NapA, which
              is associated with a small, di-haem cytochrome, NapB; a putative
