              which routinely adds nitrite to meat during the curing process
              (Tarr, 1941; Shank et al., 1962; Incze et al., 1974; Pierson and
              Smoot, 1982; DeGiusti and DeVito, 1992). However, cell-derived
              NO-related antimicrobial activity generated from the enzymatic
              oxidation of L-arginine (Chapter 4) has been recognized only
              recently to be an important component of host defense. In addition
              to indirect effects resulting from modulation of immune responses
              (Chapter 10), it is now evident that NO or its congeners can exert
