  volume   =  119,
  number   =  27,
  pages    = "e2123469119",
  abstract = "Biofilm formation is an important and ubiquitous mode of growth
              among bacteria. Central to the evolutionary advantage of biofilm
              formation is cell-cell and cell-surface adhesion achieved by a
              variety of factors, some of which are diffusible compounds that
              may operate as classical public goods-factors that are costly to
              produce but may benefit other cells. An outstanding question is
