              barrier at the cell surface and is a main contributor to the
              innate resistance that Gram-negative bacteria display against many
              antimicrobials. Not surprisingly, these important properties of
              LPS have driven a vast and still prolific body of literature for
              more than a hundred years. LPS research has also led to pioneering
              studies in bacterial envelope biogenesis and physiology, mostly
