              homeostasis requirements monitored by KdpD/KdpE and other TCSs
              such as PhoP/PhoQ are critical to survival in the stressful
              conditions encountered by pathogens during host interactions. It
              follows these TCSs may therefore acquire adaptive roles in
              response to selective pressures associated with adopting a
              pathogenic lifestyle. Given the central role of K(+) in virulence,
