              and 1-hydroxyphenazine (1-OHPHZ) generate phenazine radical
              intermediates via presumably single-electron transfer reaction
              with ferrous iron, leading to the anaerobic killing of Pseudomonas
              cells. The recA mutant defect in the DNA repair system was more
              sensitive to anaerobic conditions. Our results collectively
              suggest that both phenazines anaerobically kill cells via DNA
              damage during electron transfer with iron.",
