              Mancia, Filippo",
  journal  = "Nature",
  volume   =  604,
  number   =  7905,
  pages    = "371--376",
  abstract = "The outer membrane of Gram-negative bacteria has an external
              leaflet that is largely composed of lipopolysaccharide, which
              provides a selective permeation barrier, particularly against
              antimicrobials1. The final and crucial step in the biosynthesis of
              lipopolysaccharide is the addition of a species-dependent
              O-antigen to the lipid A core oligosaccharide, which is catalysed
