              disequilibrium with six different haplogroups present in N. crassa
              populations. Isolates from an identical cwr haplogroup show robust
              fusion, while somatic cell fusion between isolates of different
              haplogroups is significantly blocked in cell wall dissolution. The
              cwr-1 gene encodes a putative polysaccharide monooxygenase (PMO).
              Herein we confirm that CWR-1 is a C1-oxidizing chitin PMO. We show
              that the catalytic (PMO) domain of CWR-1 was sufficient for
              checkpoint function and cell fusion blockage; however, through
              analysis of active-site, histidine-brace mutants, the catalytic
