  journal  = "Structure",
  abstract = "Pseudomonas aeruginosa is an opportunistic pathogen that is
              responsible for thousands of deaths every year in the United
              States. P. aeruginosa virulence factor production is mediated by
              quorum sensing, a mechanism of bacterial cell-cell communication
              that relies on the production and detection of signal molecules
