  journal  = "mSystems",
  pages    = "e0034222",
  abstract = "Pseudomonas aeruginosa is an opportunistic pathogen that causes
              difficult-to-treat infections. Two well-studied divergent P.
              aeruginosa strain types, PAO1 and PA14, have significant genomic
              heterogeneity, including diverse accessory genes present in only
              some strains. Genome content comparisons find core genes that are
