               The synthesis and degradation of c-di-GMP in bacterial cells
               depend, respectively, on diguanylate cyclases and
               c-di-GMP-specific phosphodiesterases. Since c-di-GMP metabolic
               enzymes (CMEs) are often fused to sensory domains, their
               activities are likely controlled by environmental signals,
               thereby altering cellular c-di-GMP levels and regulating
