  number    =  10,
  pages     = "1767--1781.e6",
  abstract  = "SummaryPseudomonas aeruginosa is a common cause of pulmonary
               infection. As a Gram-negative pathogen, it can initiate a brisk
               and highly destructive inflammatory response; however, most hosts
               become tolerant to the bacterial burden, developing chronic
               infection. Using a murine model of pneumonia, we demonstrate that
               this shift from inflammation to disease tolerance is promoted by
