  journal  = "Elife",
  volume   =  10,
  abstract = "Bacteriophages can be trapped in the matrix of bacterial biofilms,
              such that the cells inside them are protected. It is not known
              whether these phages are still infectious and whether they pose a
              threat to newly arriving bacteria. Here, we address these
              questions using Escherichia coli and its lytic phage T7. Prior
              work has demonstrated that T7 phages are bound in the outermost
