               heterogeneity such as pH and oxygen gradients renders biofilms
               highly resistant to conventional antibiotics. To date,
               effectively treating biofilm infections remains a significant
               challenge. Herein, we report the fabrication of micellar
               nanoparticles adapted to heterogeneous biofilm microenvironments,
               enabling nitric oxide (NO) release through two distinct
               photoredox catalysis mechanisms. The key design feature involves
