               vacuole forming area (the naked ribbed wall). Instead of normal
               food vacuoles only narrow elongated outpocketings are formed.
               Food vacuoles which have been formed during treatment contain
               kappa symbionts. After disintegration due to digestion of the
               symbiont cells the R bodies unwind and penetrate the food vacuole
