  volume   =  10,
  pages    =  494,
  abstract = "Models to study host-pathogen interactions in vitro are an
              important tool for investigating the infectious disease process
              and evaluating the efficacy of antimicrobial compounds. In these
              models, the viability of mammalian cells is often determined using
              the lactate dehydrogenase (LDH) cytotoxicity assay. In the present
              study we evaluated whether bacteria could interfere with the LDH
