  author    = "Ludford, Paul T and Tor, Yitzhak",
  editor    = "Chenoweth, David M",
  booktitle = "Methods in Enzymology",
  publisher = "Academic Press",
  volume    =  639,
  pages     = "71--90",
  abstract  = "A fluorescence-based assay for adenosine deaminase (ADA) activity
               and inhibition, which may also be formatted as an inhibitor
               discovery assay, is described. It relies on differences in
               fluorescence between an isothiazolo-based adenosine analogs (tzA)
               and its deaminated product, the corresponding inosine derivative
               (tzI), which facilitates a real-time monitoring of enzymatic
               activity. Inhibitors are added to the enzyme–substrate reaction
               mixture at various concentrations and the fluorescence signal is
