               stress conditions. The physiological significance of GLO1
               expression in response to osmotic stress is to combat the
               increase in the levels of methylglyoxal in cells during the
               production of glycerol as a compatible osmolyte. Deficiency in
               GLO1 in S. cerevisiae causes pleiotropic phenotypes in terms of
