  volume    =  4,
  number    =  1,
  pages     =  151,
  abstract  = "Upon exposure to excessive reactive oxygen species (ROS),
               organismal survival depends on the strength of the endogenous
               antioxidant defense barriers that prevent mitochondrial and
               cellular deterioration. Previously, we showed that glycolic acid
               can restore the mitochondrial membrane potential of C. elegans
               treated with paraquat, an oxidant that produces superoxide and
               other ROS species, including hydrogen peroxide. Here, we
