  number    =  2,
  pages     = "368--381",
  abstract  = "In enterics, the transcription factor SoxR triggers a global
               stress response by sensing a broad spectrum of redox-cycling
               compounds. In the non-enteric bacteria Pseudomonas aeruginosa and
               Streptomyces coelicolor, SoxR is activated by endogenous
               redox-active small molecules and only regulates a small set of
