               of -450 to +80 mV, P. aeruginosa and S. coelicolor SoxR are less
               sensitive to viologens, which have redox potentials below -350
               mV. Using a mutagenic approach, we pinpointed three amino acids
               that contribute to the reduced sensitivity of P. aeruginosa and
               S. coelicolor SoxR. Notably these residues are not conserved in
               homologues of the Enterobacteriaceae. We further identified a
               motif within the sensor domain that tunes the activity of SoxR
