  publisher = "The Royal Society",
  volume    =  12,
  number    =  4,
  pages     =  220010,
  abstract  = "There are many reactive intermediates found in metabolic
               pathways. Could these potentially toxic molecules be exploited
               for an organism's benefit? We propose that during certain
               microbial infections, the production of inherently reactive
               aldehydes by an infected host is a previously unappreciated
               innate immune defence mechanism. While there has been a
               significant focus on the effects of aldehydes on mammalian
