  volume    =  4,
  number    =  1,
  pages     = "1--9",
  abstract  = "AbstractThe emergence and spread of bacteria resistant to
               commonly used antibiotics poses a critical threat to modern
               medical practice. Multiple classes of bacterial efflux pump
               systems play various roles in antibiotic resistance, and members
               of the resistance-nodulation-division (RND) transporter
               superfamily are among the most important determinants of
