               metabolism, which is not relevant for M. tuberculosis during
               infection. PIs induced self-poisoning of M. tuberculosis by
               promoting the accumulation of glycerol phosphate and rapid ATP
               depletion. This study underlines the importance of understanding
               central bacterial metabolism in vivo and of developing predictive
               in vitro culture conditions as a prerequisite for the rational
               discovery of new antibiotics.",
