  publisher = "Nature Publishing Group",
  pages     = "1--15",
  abstract  = "Although diet is a substantial determinant of the human gut
               microbiome, the interplay between specific foods and microbial
               community structure remains poorly understood. Coffee is a
               habitually consumed beverage with established metabolic and
               health benefits. We previously found that coffee is, among >150
