  journal   = "Free Radic. Biol. Med.",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  225,
  pages     = "910--924",
  abstract  = "As a highly contagious acute respiratory disease, influenza A
               virus (A/WSN/1933) poses a huge threat to human health and public
               health. influenza A virus proliferation relies on glucose
               metabolism in host cells, yet the effects of influenza A virus on
               glucose metabolism and the underlying molecular mechanisms remain
