               various sensing and information processing modules. A whole-cell
               bioelectronic sensor with a T7 RNAP-based signal amplifier was
               first constructed that detected mercury contaminants below the
               level of WHO safe limit for drinking water. We demonstrated the
               modularity and programmability of the sensor design by
