               inactivation of the lrrkA gene, which encodes a protein with a
               kinase domain and leucine-rich repeats. LrrkA knockout (KO) cells
               kill ingested Klebsiella pneumoniae bacteria inefficiently. This
               defect is not additive to the killing defect observed in kil2 KO
