  volume    =  15,
  number    =  8,
  pages     = "e0082724",
  abstract  = "Grazing of amoebae on microorganisms represents one of the oldest
               predator-prey dynamic relationships in nature. It represents a
               genetic ``melting pot'' for an ancient and continuous
               multi-directional inter- and intra-kingdom horizontal gene
               transfer between amoebae and its preys, intracellular microbial
               residents, endosymbionts, and giant viruses, which has shaped the
               evolution, selection, and adaptation of microbes that evade
