               heterologous reporter assays. These results confirm that the
               binding of PqsE to RhlR is able to fine-tune RhlR transcription
               factor activity in a promoter-specific manner and prove that this
               ability is independent of other factors present in P. aeruginosa
               . IMPORTANCE Pseudomonas aeruginosa is an opportunistic human
               pathogen that can cause fatal infections. There exists an urgent
               need for new, effective antimicrobial agents to combat P.
               aeruginosa . The PqsE-RhlR protein-protein interaction is
