  volume    =  42,
  number    =  3,
  pages     =  120,
  abstract  = "Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a major opportunistic pathogen,
               especially involved with nosocomial infections. Siderophores such
               as pyoverdine are crucial for iron acquisition in bacteria and
               play an important role in virulence regulation. Therefore,
               targeting siderophore pathways has been suggested as a potential
