              perturbed the expression of a key regulatory gene (fruA) by
              constructing independent in-frame deletions of four trans acting
              regulatory loci that modify its expression. While mutants retained
              developmental capability, the deletions caused changes in the
              expression of fruA and a dramatic shortening of time required for
              completion of development. We found phenotypic changes in the
              majority of traits measured, indicating pleiotropic effects of
              changes in regulation. The magnitude of the change for different
              traits was variable but the extent of differences between the
              mutants and parental type were consistent with changes in fruA
              expression. We conclude that changes in the expression of
              essential regulatory regions of developmental networks may
