              we developed a program, sRNAPredict2, that identifies putative
              sRNAs by searching for co-localization of genetic features
              commonly associated with sRNA-encoding genes. Using sRNAPredict2,
              we conducted genome-wide annotations for putative sRNA-encoding
              genes in the intergenic regions of 11 diverse pathogens. In total,
              2759 previously unannotated candidate sRNA loci were predicted.
