              the different pathogens analyzed, raising the possibility that
              there are species-specific differences in the reliance on
              sRNA-mediated regulation. Of 34 previously unannotated sRNAs
              predicted in the opportunistic pathogen Pseudomonas aeruginosa, 31
              were experimentally tested and 17 were found to encode sRNA
              transcripts. Our findings suggest that numerous genes have been
              missed in the current annotations of bacterial genomes and that,
              by using improved bioinformatic approaches and tools, much remains
