              nutrient gradients and microenvironments. Here we show how the
              response of the sulfur-oxidizing bacterium Thiovulum majus to
              changing oxygen gradients causes cells to organize into
              large-scale fronts. To study this phenomenon, we develop a
              technique to isolate and enrich these bacteria from the
              environment. Using this enrichment culture, we observe the
