  pages    = "430--437",
  abstract = "Circadian rhythms are 24h oscillations in physiology and behavior
              which allow organisms to anticipate and adapt to daily demands
              associated with the day/night cycle. The currently accepted model
              of the molecular clockwork is described as a transcriptional
              process composed of negative regulatory feedback loops. However,
              ample evidence underlines the important contribution of
