              Era (approximately 1.9 Gya) and the second during the late
              Neoproterozoic and early Paleozoic eras (0.6-0.45 Gya). Each size
              step required a major innovation in organismal complexity--first
              the eukaryotic cell and later eukaryotic multicellularity. These
              size steps coincide with, or slightly postdate, increases in the
              concentration of atmospheric oxygen, suggesting latent
              evolutionary potential was realized soon after environmental
              limitations were removed.",
