  pages    = "573--578",
  abstract = "Bacteria communicate via small diffusible molecules and thereby
              mediate group-coordinated behavior, a process referred to as
              quorum sensing. The prototypical quorum sensing system found in
              Gram-negative bacteria consists of a LuxI-type autoinducer
              synthase that produces N-acyl homoserine lactones (AHLs) as
