              detects endogenously produced α-pyrones that serve as signaling
              molecules at low nanomolar concentrations. Additionally, the
              ketosynthase PpyS was identified as pyrone synthase.
              Reconstitution of the entire system containing PluR, the
              PluR-target operon we termed pcf and PpyS in Escherichia coli
              demonstrated that the cell-cell communication circuit is portable.
              Our research thus deorphanizes a signaling system and suggests
              that additional modes of bacterial communication may await
              discovery.",
