              subclone assignments), multilocus sequence typing, gyrA and parC
              sequence (fluoroquinolone resistance-determining loci), and
              pulsed-field gel electrophoresis. RESULTS: Of the recent
              fluoroquinolone-resistant clinical isolates, 52\% represented a
              single ST131 subclonal lineage, H30, which expanded abruptly after
              2000. This subclone had a unique and conserved gyrA/parC allele
              combination, supporting its tight clonality. Unlike other ST131
              subclones, H30 was significantly associated with fluoroquinolone
              resistance and was the most prevalent subclone among current E.
