  number   =  5,
  pages    = "E597--605",
  abstract = "Microbial quiescence and slow growth are ubiquitous physiological
              states, but their study is complicated by low levels of metabolic
              activity. To address this issue, we used a time-selective
              proteome-labeling method [bioorthogonal noncanonical amino acid
              tagging (BONCAT)] to identify proteins synthesized preferentially,
              but at extremely low rates, under anaerobic survival conditions by
              the opportunistic pathogen Pseudomonas aeruginosa. One of these
