  volume   =  6,
  pages    =  1099,
  abstract = "The success of Pseudomonas species as opportunistic pathogens
              derives in great part from their ability to form stable biofilms
              that offer protection against chemical and mechanical attack. The
              extracellular matrix of biofilms contains numerous biomolecules,
              and it has recently been discovered that in Pseudomonas one of the
              components includes β-sheet rich amyloid fibrils (functional
              amyloid) produced by the fap operon. However, the role of the
              functional amyloid within the biofilm has not yet been
