  pages    = "255--265",
  abstract = "Bacteria use complex strategies to coordinate
              temperature-dependent gene expression. Many genes encoding heat
              shock proteins and virulence factors are regulated by
              temperature-sensing RNA sequences, known as RNA thermometers
              (RNATs), in their mRNAs. For these genes, the 5' untranslated
              region of the mRNA folds into a structure that blocks ribosome
              access at low temperatures. Increasing the temperature gradually
              shifts the equilibrium between the closed and open conformations
