  journal  = "Curr. Opin. Microbiol.",
  volume   =  11,
  number   =  2,
  pages    = "161--167",
  abstract = "The ecological and evolutionary roles of antibiotics have been
              usually inferred from their therapeutical activity. Since those
              compounds inhibit bacterial growth, it was thought that they
              should be produced by soil microorganisms to inhibit the growth of
              competitors in natural habitats. It has been shown however that
              antibiotics modulate transcription of bacteria in a dose dependent
              manner. Furthermore, each antibiotic triggers a specific response,
              and those responses may have adaptive values. From these
              observations, it has been suggested that antibiotics may have a
              role as signalling molecules besides inhibitors. The facts that a
