              swarming cooperation. Our analysis shows that multilevel selection
              can favor costly swarming cooperation because it causes population
              expansion. However, due to high costs and diminishing returns
              constitutive cooperation can only be favored by natural selection
              when relatedness is high. Regulated expression of cooperative
