  abstract = "Metabolic engineering studies have generally focused on
              manipulating enzyme levels through either the amplification,
              addition, or deletion of a particular pathway. However, with
              cofactor-dependent production systems, once the enzyme levels are
              no longer limiting, cofactor availability and the ratio of the
              reduced to oxidized form of the cofactor can become limiting.
