              Structure 10, 1349-1361, [1]), is very flexible and adopts
              different conformations depending on the bound ligand. Some PAS
              sequences present in the PFAM database did not produce a good
              structural model, even after realignment using a structure-based
              alignment method, suggesting that these representatives are
              unlikely to have a fold resembling any of the structural
              prototypes of the PAS domain superfamily.",
