  pages    = "79--85",
  abstract = "Nitric oxide (NO) is increased in the exhaled air of some patients
              with inflammatory lung disorders, but not in others. NO may
              combine with superoxide to form peroxynitrite, which lowers NO gas
              concentrations, increases formation of nitrate, and increases
              nitration of tyrosine residues on proteins. We hypothesized that
