              myeloperoxidase and murine lung epithelial cells did not
              demonstrate a reduction of NO gas with nitrotyrosine or an
              increase in nitrate formation. These data demonstrate that nitrate
              and nitrotyrosine are elevated in the sputa of CF subjects and
              suggest increased production of NO in the lower respiratory tract
              of CF patients, despite the relatively low exhaled NO levels.
              Pediatr Pulmonol. 2000; 30:79-85. Published 2000 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
