  abstract = "Riboswitches are structured noncoding RNA domains that selectively
              bind metabolites and control gene expression (Mandal and Breaker
              2004a; Coppins et al. 2007; Roth and Breaker 2009). Nearly all
              examples of the known riboswitches reside in noncoding regions of
              messenger RNAs where they control transcription or translation.
