              about three per year (Ames and Breaker 2009), and these have been
              shown to selectively respond to fundamental metabolites including
              coenzymes, nucleobases or their derivatives, amino acids, and
              other small molecule ligands. The characteristics of some
              riboswitches suggest they could be modern descendents of an
              ancient sensory and regulatory system that likely functioned
              before the emergence of enzymes and genetic factors made of
              protein (Nahvi et al. 2002; Vitreschak et al. 2004; Breaker 2006).
