               Murakami, Keiji and Harrison, Joe J and Colvin, Kelly M and
               Parsek, Matthew R",
  booktitle = "Biofilm Infections",
  publisher = "Springer, New York, NY",
  pages     = "251--266",
  abstract  = "The field of biofilm microbiology, while by no means new, has
               been experiencing significant “growing pains” as more and more
               researchers become involved. One of the underlying reasons is the
               lack of standardized methods for culturing biofilm communities.
               Many times, the culturing format will be unique to the study in
               question, resulting in difficulties when other labs attempt to
               confirm results produced by another lab. Another issue has been
               the limited utility of different culturing methods for the
