  number   =  14,
  pages    = "E1419--27",
  abstract = "Generation of genetic diversity is a prerequisite for bacterial
              evolution and adaptation. Short-term diversification and selection
              within populations is, however, largely uncharacterised, as
              existing studies typically focus on fixed substitutions. Here, we
