              currently known multidrug transporters in bacteria. Based on
              energetics and structural characteristics, the bacterial multidrug
              transporters can be classified into five distinct families.
              Functional reconstitution in liposomes of purified multidrug
              transport proteins from four families revealed that these proteins
              are capable of mediating the export of structurally unrelated
              drugs independent of accessory proteins or cytoplasmic components.
