              safety climate (OR, 1.88; P=.004; 95\% CI: 1.21-2.91) among
              others. CONCLUSION: The prevalence of PI was substantial.
              Underreporting rates and risk factors for exposure were similar to
              those identified in other RN work populations, although factors
              uniquely associated with home care were also identified. Risk
              mitigation strategies tailored to home care are needed to reduce
              risk of exposure in this setting.",
