  volume   =  13,
  number   =  4,
  pages    = "1095--1105",
  abstract = "Chronic polymicrobial lung infections are the chief complication
              in patients with cystic fibrosis. The dominant pathogen in
              late-stage disease is Pseudomonas aeruginosa, which forms
              recalcitrant, structured communities known as biofilms. Many
              aspects of biofilm biology are poorly understood; consequently,
