              for methylation at the C-2 position in hopanoids. This gene is
              found in several, but not all, cyanobacteria and also in alpha
              -proteobacteria and acidobacteria. Thus, one cannot extrapolate
              from the presence of 2-methylhopanes alone, in modern environments
