              operator DNA, and after light exposure. These structures provide
              visualizations of how adenosylcobalamin mediates CarH tetramer
              formation in the dark, how this tetramer binds to the promoter -35
              element to repress transcription, and how light exposure leads to
              a large-scale conformational change that activates transcription.
