  pages    = "1244--1254",
  abstract = "Many bacterial lineages lack seemingly essential metabolic genes.
              Previous work suggested selective benefits could drive the loss of
              biosynthetic functions from bacterial genomes when the
              corresponding metabolites are sufficiently available in the
              environment. However, the factors that govern this ``genome
              streamlining'' remain poorly understood. Here we determine the
              effect of plasticity and epistasis on the fitness of Escherichia
              coli genotypes from whose genome biosynthetic genes for one, two,
