              part of an ecosystem restoration project. Martha's Vineyard was
              home to the last remaining heath hen population until its
              extinction in 1932. We conducted this study to aid in determining
              the suitability of greater prairie chickens as a possible
              replacement for the heath hen. We examined mitochondrial control
              region sequences from extant populations of all prairie grouse
