  pages    = "848--852",
  abstract = "Many bacteria on earth exist in surface-attached communities known
              as biofilms. These films are responsible for manifold problems,
              including hospital-acquired infections and biofouling, but they
              can also be beneficial. Biofilm growth depends on the transport of
              nutrients and waste, for which diffusion is thought to be the main
