              mathematical models and simulations were developed to explain the
              development, structures, and interactions of biofilms. The forces
              determining the spatial structure of biofilms, including
              microcolonies, extracellular polymeric substances (EPS), and
              channels, are still the subject of controversy. To achieve
              conclusive explanations for the structures observed in biofilms
              the cooperation of both fields of investigation, modelling and
              experimental research, is necessary. The expanding field of
              molecular techniques not only allows more and more detailed
              documentation of the spatial distribution of species, but also of
              functional activities of single cells in their biofilm
