              activation of the HIF-1 complex (hypoxia-inducible complex-1), a
              transcriptional activator that controls the expression of most of
              hypoxia-regulated genes. HIF-1 complex is overexpressed in a
              variety of tumours and its expression appears to correlate with
              poor prognosis and responses to chemo or radiotherapy. Thus,
