  pages    = "310--319",
  abstract = "It is established that prion protein is the sole causative agent
              in a number of diseases in humans and animals. However, the nature
              of conformational changes that the normal cellular form, PrP(C),
              undergoes in its conversion to a self-replicating state is still
              not fully understood. The ordered C-terminus of PrP(C) proteins
