              binds both Gag and mature CA proteins, the two binding
              interactions are actually different. Tryptophan 121 (W121) in CyP
              A distinguished the two proteins: a phenylalanine substitution
              (W121F) impaired binding of mature CA protein but not of Gag. This
              indicates the occurrence of a maturation-dependent switch in the
