  abstract = "Nitrous oxide (N(2)O) is an important greenhouse gas (GHG) which
              has a global warming potential 310 times that of carbon dioxide
              (CO(2)) over a hundred year lifespan. N(2)O is generated during
              microbial nitrification and denitrification, which are common in
