              cycle, with the ability to germinate, grow, and subsequently
              sporulate in both the liquid SESOM extract and in ASM inserted
              into wells in agar medium. Cells grew in liquid SESOM without
              separating, forming multicellular structures that coalesced to
              form clumps and encasing the ensuing spores in an extracellular
              matrix. Bacillus was able to translocate from the point of
              inoculation through soil microcosms as shown by the emergence of
              outgrowths on the surrounding agar surface. Microscopic inspection
              revealed bundles of parallel chains inside the soil. The motility
