              dehydrogenase (SDH). When cells are grown under low light, both
              complexes are concentrated in discrete patches in the thylakoid
              membranes, about 100-300 nm in diameter and containing tens to
              hundreds of complexes. Exposure to moderate light leads to
              redistribution of both NDH-1 and SDH such that they become evenly
              distributed within the thylakoid membranes. The effects of
