              occurred at the level of intercellular accumulation and not
              primary attachment. Mutation of fnbA or fnbB alone did not
              substantially affect biofilm, and expression of either gene alone
              from a complementing plasmid in fnbA fnbB mutants restored biofilm
              formation. FnBP-promoted biofilm was dependent on the integrity of
