              substrates. Substrate-dependent induction of vexRAB was dependent
              on vexR and episomal vexR expression provided a growth advantage
              in the presence of the VexAB substrate deoxycholate. The
              expression of vexRAB increased, in a vexR-dependent manner, in
              response to the loss of RND efflux activity. This suggested that
              VexAB may function to export intracellular metabolites. Support
