              dbv37) and of six operons (dbv2-dbv1, dbv14-dbv8, dbv17-dbv15,
              dbv21-dbv20, dbv24-dbv28, and dbv30-dbv35). We propose a complex
              and coordinated model of regulation in which Dbv3 directly or
              indirectly activates transcription of dbv4 and controls
              biosynthesis of 4-hydroxyphenylglycine and the heptapeptide
              backbone, A40926 export, and some tailoring reactions
              (mannosylation and hexose oxidation), while Dbv4 directly
              regulates biosynthesis of 3,5-dihydroxyphenylglycine and other
              tailoring reactions, including the four cross-links, halogenation,
              glycosylation, and acylation. IMPORTANCE: This report expands
              knowledge of the regulatory mechanisms used to control the
              biosynthesis of the glycopeptide antibiotic A40926 in the
              actinomycete Nonomuraea sp. strain ATCC 39727. A40926 is the
