  abstract = "The branched respiratory chain of Pseudomonas aeruginosa contains
              at least two terminal oxidases which are active under normal
              physiological conditions. One of these, cytochrome co, is a
              cytochrome c oxidase which is completely inhibited by
              concentrations of the respiratory inhibitor potassium cyanide as
