              replicating and catalytic macromolecules could become encapsulated
              in the vesicles. In the laboratory, this can be modeled by
              encapsulated polymerases prepared as liposomes. By an appropriate
              choice of lipids, the permeability properties of the liposomes can
              be adjusted so that ionic substrates permeate at a sufficient rate
              to provide a source of monomers for the enzymes, with the result
              that nucleic acids accumulate in the vesicles. Despite this
