  abstract = "The FixL protein of Bradyrhizobium japonicum is a dimeric oxygen
              sensor responsible for initiating regulation of transcription of
              genes encoding proteins involved in nitrogen fixation and
              oxidative stress. It consists of an N-terminal heme-bound PAS
              domain, denoted bjFixLH, and a C-terminal histidine kinase domain
