              and OmpU. Changes in the osmolarity of a tryptone-based medium
              also produced coordinate changes in the expression of these
              proteins. Other environmental signals (temperature and pH) had a
              more pronounced effect on the expression of cholera toxin and TcpA
              than they did on the outer membrane proteins. These results
