              observed in soils with high carbon-to-nitrogen ratios and in soils
              from cold climatic regions. After 90 days, microbial community
              responses increased the temperature sensitivity of respiration in
              high-latitude soils by a factor of 1.4 compared to the
              instantaneous temperature response. This suggests that the
