  volume   =  42,
  number   =  17,
  pages    = "10987--10999",
  abstract = "Transcription by RNA polymerase may be interrupted by pauses
              caused by backtracking or misincorporation that can be resolved by
              the conserved bacterial Gre-factors. However, the consequences of
              such pausing in the living cell remain obscure. Here, we developed
              molecular biology and transcriptome sequencing tools in the human
              pathogen Streptococcus pneumoniae and provide evidence that
              transcription elongation is rate-limiting on highly expressed
              genes. Our results suggest that transcription elongation may be a
              highly regulated step of gene expression in S. pneumoniae.
