              dual proteomics approach consisting of gel-based and gel-free
              comparisons were undertaken to analyse protein profiles in a
              transmissible, early (acute) isolate of the Australian epidemic
              strain 1 (AES-1R), the virulent burns/wound isolate PA14, and the
              poorly virulent, laboratory-associated strain PAO1. Over 1700 P.
              aeruginosa proteins were confidently identified. AES-1R protein
              profiles revealed elevated abundance of proteins associated with
