              acidic side chains at the midsection of the structure, termed the
              ``anion stripe''. In addition, many surface-exposed salt bridges
              likely contribute to the stabilization of the postfusion structure
              at low pH. These results provide structural insights into the
              mechanism of MARV GP2-mediated membrane fusion.",
