              NsrR/DNA interactions were thoroughly analysed in vitro. Using
              EMSA analysis, NsrR::FLAG was shown to interact with predicted
              operators in the norB, aniA and nsrR upstream regions with a K(d)
              of 7, 19 and 35 nM respectively. DNase I footprint analysis was
              performed on the upstream regions of norB and nsrR, where NsrR was
              shown to protect the predicted 29 bp binding sites. The presence
              of exogenously added NO inhibited DNA binding by NsrR. Alanine
