  pages    = "2453--2463",
  abstract = "Untargeted profiling of small-molecule metabolites from microbial
              culture supernatants (metabolic footprinting) has great potential
              as a phenotyping tool. We used time-resolved metabolic
              footprinting to compare one Escherichia coli and three Pseudomonas
              aeruginosa strains growing on complex media and show that
              considering metabolite changes over the whole course of growth
