  number   =  7,
  pages    = "958--970",
  abstract = "Complex I or NADH quinone oxidoreductase (NUO) is an integral
              component of modern day respiratory chains and has a close
              evolutionary relationship with energy-conserving
              [NiFe]-hydrogenases of anaerobic microorganisms. Specifically, in
