              because of their abundance and the availability of an easy assay
              to follow purification. Permeases, even if abundant, require
              reconstitution into liposomes before their activities can be
              measured. Second, the introduction of recombinant DNA
              methodologies has provided an explosion of information on the
              primary structures of transport proteins. This has allowed their
              grouping into protein families and the development of models for
              their structures and mechanisms. A mutational analysis has been
              performed with the cloned plasma membrane H + -ATPase, and it has
              provided insights about functional domains and physiological roles
              of the enzyme. A similar analysis has been started with the
              vacuolar H + -ATPase. Finally, electrophysiological methodologies
