              molecular level. In particular, patch clamping has allowed the
              identification for the first time of ion channels in yeast. These
              novel developments constitute the basis for the present chapter,
              which attempts to complement the review by Cooper (1982). Some
              classic aspects not previously covered are also briefly...",
