              temperatures suggested additional translational control. We
              conducted a comprehensive structural and functional analysis of
              the 5' untranslated regions of the ibpA genes from P. putida and
              Pseudomonas aeruginosa. Both contain a ROSE-type RNA thermometer
              that is substantially shorter and simpler than previously reported
              ROSE elements. Comprised of two hairpin structures only, they
              inhibit translation at low temperature and permit translation
