              found that sodC, the gene that encodes the periplasmic SOD of
              Escherichia coli, is repressed anaerobically by Fnr and is among
              the many antioxidant genes that are induced in stationary phase by
              RpoS. Surprisingly, the entry of wild-type E. coli into stationary
              phase is accompanied by a several-hour-long period of acute
              sensitivity to hydrogen peroxide. Induction of the RpoS regulon
