              Salmonella typhimurium that lacked CuZnSOD were not detectably
              sensitive to exogenous superoxide, both were killed more rapidly
              than their parent strains by exogenous hydrogen peroxide in early
              stationary phase. This sensitivity required prior growth in air.
              Evidently, periplasmic superoxide is generated during stationary
