              activity in spite of some reduction in viability. Exposure of
              gonococci to 1.0 mM hydrogen peroxide made the organisms
              significantly more resistant to higher concentrations of hydrogen
              peroxide and to neutrophils than control organisms. These results
              suggest that catalase is an important defense for N. gonorrhoeae
              during attack by human neutrophils. The rapid response of this
