              respiration. However, direct electron transfer by cell-cell
              contact is important as well. This review addresses the mechanisms
              of exocellular electron transfer in anaerobic microbial
              communities. There are fundamental differences but also
              similarities between electron transfer to another microorganism or
              to an insoluble electron acceptor. The physical separation of the
              electron donor and electron acceptor metabolism allows energy
