              cycles on the planet's surface. Although the evolutionary history
              of the amino acid sequences in the oxidoreductases is very
              difficult to reconstruct due to gene duplication and horizontal
              gene transfer, the evolution of the folds in the catalytic sites
              can potentially be used to infer the history of these enzymes.
