  volume   =  486,
  pages    = "369--385",
  abstract = "The overarching goal herein was to develop a protocol that could
              be used to generate consistent information on the generation and
              emission of nitrous oxide (N(2)O) from open-surface wastewater
              treatment bioreactors. The developed protocol was reviewed and
              endorsed by the United States Environmental Protection Agency
              (USEPA), whereupon it was used to determine N(2)O emissions from a
              wide array of wastewater treatment processes across the United
              States. Scaled-down variants of the protocol have also since been
